      "text": "so that the monotonicity of the operator III may not true in general and depends on the dynamics of the endogenous signal g. The particular case where dgt = g′(t)dt with g′ ≥ 0 (i.e., g is a nondecreasing input curve) and h′ is nonincreasing (i.e., the impact function h is concave on the real line) would yield the monotonicity of III, but such assumptions may be too restrictive.",
